tput (original token count: 15831)\nTotal output lines: 2\n\n{\"status\":\"fulfilled\",\"value\":{\"chunk_id\":\"67183f\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000003916,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":11996,\"output\":\"# Experiment SOP (portable)\\n\\nA generalizable standard operating procedure for AI-assisted research experiments. Drop this file into any project and reference it from that project's `CLAUDE.md` (e.g. \\\"Follow `worklog/experiment_SOP.md` for all experiment work\\\"). Written for Claude Code, but the roles are model-agnostic.\\n\\n## Roles (three-model separation of duties)\\n\\n| Role | Who | Duty |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| **Planner / Analyst** | The main-session model (strongest reasoning tier; currently Claude Fable 5.1) | Writes plans, judges reliability, writes analyses. Does NOT write implementation code directly. |\\n| **Coder** | The strongest coding model at its highest reasoning setting — **currently Claude Opus 5 at max effort, a separate subagent launched from the main session (Agent tool, model `opus`) working in a dedicated git worktree (per Yixun 2026-09-15; 2026-09-12 → 2026-09-15 it was OpenAI Codex `gpt-6-astra` at Ultra via `codex exec`; before that a Claude Opus 4.8 max-effort subagent)** | Implements exactly what the approved plan specifies. |\\n| **Reviewer** | **The opposite model family from the Coder** (mandatory cross-model review; see reciprocity note below). | Reviews all newly written code; review is saved, not just read. If the reviewer is unavailable, say so — never silently substitute. |\\n\\n> **Reviewer reciprocity — no model reviews its own code.** The Reviewer is always the opposite model family from the **Coder**. With the current roles (Planner Claude Fable 5.1, Coder Claude Opus 5; per Yixun 2026-09-15), the code Reviewer is **OpenAI Codex `gpt-6-astra` at Ultra** (`codex exec -s read-only` in the worktree; its final message is saved as the review file with <truncated omitted_approx_tokens=\"9039\" />atch/implementation settings (test 16).\\n- Parity validity (A1): a replicated cell requires identical per-query validity masks between the run and exp_03 on the compared population; a mismatch labels the cell 'nonreplication (validity mismatch)'; fixture with one nonzero-angle NaN.\\n- Ratio (A3): observed Δ == 0 → null point ratio with reason before any division; headline multiple only when convergence passes AND denominator status agrees across seeds 0 and 1, else 'unresolved Monte Carlo uncertainty'; fixtures for both.\\n- `log_mse` (A4) = per-query mean over [F, T] of (out − log(tgt_spec + 1e-8))², as in `eval_yaw_rotation.spectral_metrics`; `per_sample_losses` gives only loss/stft/decay.\\n- `tools/exp10_compare.py` and `tools/exp10_summarize.py` per §5/§6; the summariser's bootstrap must follow §4 exactly (shared mask, one index draw per replicate for Δ*, G*, R*, status rules incl. exact-zero draws counted, room bootstrap with multiplicities, seed-1 convergence). Figure per §5 (FLAC style: see `/home/yixunhu/codespace/FLAC/analysis/pilot_study/plot_pilot_yaw_gaps.py` for the look, read-only) with the historical band labelled \\\"context only\\\".\\n\\nVerification to report: `python -m pytest tests/test_exp10_*.py -q -p no:cacheprovider`; `tests/test_exp03_record_tools.py` and `tests/test_exp04_record_tools.py` still green (pins untouched); `python -m py_compile` on the new files; `git diff --check`; the smoke `python tools/exp10_yaw_pilot.py --arm smoke --backbone simple --checkpoint checkpoints/xRIR_unseen.pth --manifest ckpt/yaw_rotation/reference_manifest.json --manifest-hash 47637a55ccc594a32c35362f970e25296e352ccc81778f9523ce882ff930153d --num-shot 8 --ks 0,64,128,256,384 --batches 0 --controls --device cpu --out-dir <tmp>` (report elapsed and that k = 0 gaps are 0, controls match to 1e-6). Final report: commit SHAs with one-line descriptions, test counts, the smoke's meta.json, and any deviation from the plan with its reason.\\n\"}}\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"\n[7] tool exec call: text(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"sed -n '1,220p' /home/yixunhu/codespace/xRIR_code/worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_10_yaw_pilot_claude/plan_yaw_pilot.md\",\"max_output_tokens\":18000}));\ntext(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"rg --files -g AGENTS.md -g 'python*' /home/yixunhu/codespace 2>/dev/null | head -60 && command -v python && python --version && ls -ld ckpt checkpoints /home/yixunhu/miniconda3/envs/xRIR/bin/python /home/yixunhu/anaconda3/envs/xRIR/bin/python 2>/dev/null && ps -eo pid,pcpu,pmem,args --sort=-pcpu | head -12\",\"max_output_tokens\":3000}));\n\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"\n[8] tool exec result: Script completed\nWall time 0.2 seconds\nOutput:\n\n{\"chunk_id\":\"c66f02\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000007193,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":7261,\"output\":\"# Plan — exp_10 `yaw_pilot` (xRIR analogue of FLAC exp_02 `yaw_noninvariance`)\\n\\n**Planner:** Claude Fable 5.1 (session xrir-code-25). **Coder:** Claude Opus 5 (Agent, worktree `xRIR_code_wt10`, branch `exp10-yaw-pilot`). **Reviewer:** OpenAI Codex `gpt-6-astra` at **ultra** (SOP setting; round 1 ran at xhigh, see §10). **Date:** 2026-09-26. **Status:** **v3.1 — APPROVED WITH CHANGES** by the round-3 review at ultra (`yaw_pilot_codex_plan_review_round3.md`; its 3 should-fixes + 1 nit are the binding amendments A1–A4 of §12). v3 was the round-2 revision at ultra (`yaw_pilot_codex_plan_review_round2.md`, REQUEST CHANGES, 1 blocker + 5 should-fixes + 2 nits; §11 maps them); v2 was the round-1 revision (`yaw_pilot_codex_plan_review.md`; §10). v1 kept as `plan_yaw_pilot_v1_superseded.md`.\\n\\n## 1. Question and stance\\n\\n**Question (Yixun, 2026-09-26).** Mimicking FLAC's exp_02 pilot: when the *conditioning* of the released xRIR checkpoint is yaw-rotated on the AcousticRooms unseen split, how much does the **prediction itself move** (Metric 1, P_α vs P_0, no GT) compared with how much **accuracy vs GT changes** (Metric 2)? FLAC's finding: \\\"predictions move ~5× more than net accuracy loses\\\".\\n\\n**Stance.** A **descriptive pilot**, like FLAC's: paired means with query-level bootstrap intervals; no confirmatory hypotheses (exp_03 already ran the Bonferroni-adjusted H1/H2 tests on Metric 2 for K = 8). Pre-registered readouts, per arm, angle and metric:\\n\\n- **R1** signed accuracy change Δ(α) = mean(e_α − e_0) vs GT, and prediction shift G(α) = mean(g_α), each with a 95 % paired query-level percentile bootstrap interval, on the **shared comparison mask** of §4; paired-valid count and exclusions reported.\\n- **R2** the ratio R = G/Δ, from the **same resamples**, with an explicit **st<truncated omitted_approx_tokens=\"6456\" />match)\\\" and is listed in the results. The historical Δ comparison population is the common-finite rows of that identical mask. Test: a fixture with one nonzero-angle NaN whose numerical differences would otherwise pass must be flagged.\\n- **A2 — execution identity (§5).** Two identifiers in meta and inside `per_sample.json`: `protocol_id` = sha256 over the complete protocol (checkpoint sha256, manifest hash, gl_seed, K, device, cudnn/TF32 flags, batch size and canonical padding, torch/numpy versions, sha256 of `tools/exp10_yaw_pilot.py`) and `execution_id` = a uuid4 + start timestamp minted once per `run`. Δ, G and R are computed from **one** `per_sample.json` whose `execution_id` matches its `meta.json` and whose bound waveform arrays' sha256s match. The summariser refuses (test 16) two executions with identical configuration, and same-device runs whose batch or implementation settings differ.\\n- **A3 — ratio point estimate and convergence (§1, §4).** If the observed Δ is exactly 0, the point ratio is null with reason \\\"observed Δ = 0\\\" (before any division); a headline multiple requires bound convergence **and** identical denominator status under seeds 0 and 1, otherwise the cell reports \\\"unresolved Monte Carlo uncertainty\\\". Fixtures for both.\\n- **A4 — `log_mse` contract (§4).** `log_mse` is exp_03's per-query mean over [F, T] of `(out − log(tgt_spec + 1e-8))²` (`eval_yaw_rotation.spectral_metrics`, not `per_sample_losses`, which returns loss / stft / decay only).\\n\"}\n{\"chunk_id\":\"862100\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000005847,\"exit_code\":2,\"original_token_count\":89,\"output\":\"/home/yixunhu/miniconda3/bin/python\\nPython 3.13.11\\nlrwxrwxrwx 1 yixunhu yixunhu  9 Apr 25 17:07 /home/yixunhu/miniconda3/envs/xRIR/bin/python -> python3.8\\nlrwxrwxrwx 1 yixunhu yixunhu 45 Sep 26 17:25 checkpoints -> /home/yixunhu/codespace/xRIR_code/checkpoints\\nlrwxrwxrwx 1 yixunhu yixunhu 38 Sep 26 17:25 ckpt -> /home/yixunhu/codespace/xRIR_code/ckpt\\n\"}\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"\n[9] tool spawn_agent call: {\"task_name\":\"bootstrap_review\",\"message\":\"gAAAAABquEsE8vlShg0tp956fJ4tMIJrsP78dtgmoGvB2H-3bjjHR230OhU5EeRybj9OUrDht3jekFxua9xl7UHg1Z3Jkrv6iF9c83Dn4hZe2-JZfq5vbhWtNFJA3DtiFkjfNqLtovZjPl_ziCL7Ot250CpTmzSZ3UI-q6iB-Im-hAkBnkAd9I3R0Xi8821tVcEP0fMQrs9upWO6p3eAzJcFG5OaVzHOTDtgc4MA7wZKrHr9AJcxE0VvHp1JrAW2fSi4lHAblaUr-I4JVihGt719d0MUDMZqIzMQCMtqEZfAVGVQOXUv69wDU6LnYGzDwbUT8QcTN7VtMZw8sv-EtUZo_N4IwwC3-KennSdmzxW7JnvVjNica85-GKbg5RV9RhmSMQsWEtEEiV7PrhNUQkmyjFHJXQ6q7bTCBep9LLfo2-bHgNUt-oVea9Eh90vUwKNo7T2fp_kk4HHhi3XuJUUHxb9pwffFjwcd1Ts7gTJmQVe8pEZxBTYOjRY_6NDik_BOYw2Z992e2qNxLgrPQRgxypCXs81ru0CFd0BkLLAt5M1jWKOtEsEk5zTmG3sYQalkpDLnb39ZFMj3BPpIQ7iU0pRBwEi6IBCS_I_56QQulSL5hQQcrxu53oUig62ngRQdQzPKO-Ma9wFFkUeEBPbYYKZ_kvjD2ka_63vhjg7hux0VrWIKLRF_V0k3t0EVJbQKcBQnRbYR_cogqaoSAtt6KBE1x8nc_mvd25N4Qzzj_h7dfB1eFLrIDPQ8Z98svm9h9QPvKhVOInbBNeHs6F-FLzslxgltJdqqSWlPekgSsJrDjLFmuxGxkio6Em06rVy23DpWn1tkVjgcDfZwYKYdvfCMzooLpsfHh4HFDdgkem-eV9nOfF5s15WElpvzrdCGMZuLWC_UPFLs1PLwgpbhGwR7W36-gSt6aYPzSDgFwOMDbD9ufUDJi0iYOKXMiRAdnotIDbp_sjhkkF-oksWpM46ZUInizpA6ZzYjTUzcjdaRbjZk25hCkl0mUOCW73z-7Pw10K076ETqghei2ZX-ceSYtTaMxssR8aw8cknfi704OHWfl6qAp_9SfuIJ2oMiHCzAM0sto5oi6es_1vEkBeXHymQoPoIQNrVyvdz_3MwCQMHko_qvt52W2hVPlxkWmpaMu1_j\"}\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"\n[10] tool 