ing historical angle `128`, or just its required C50 metric, independently produces `ok=True`. This contradicts §7’s binding criteria for every requested angle and required metric. **Minimal fix:** fail/refuse when any requested angle or required parity metric is missing; keep optional diagnostic metrics distinguishable.\n\n3. **Should-fix — comparator reports are not strict JSON.** `tools/exp10_compare.py:421` uses default `allow_nan=True`. With an all-invalid common population, `_parity_cell` includes NaN paired deltas/sign agreement, and the actual written report contains `NaN`; a strict JSON parser rejects it. **Minimal fix:** recursively replace nonfinite values with null and serialize with `allow_nan=False`, with an empty-common-mask regression.\n\n**Verified**\n\n- `tests/test_exp10_compare.py`: **23 passed**, Python 3.8, CPU only.\n- Actual `verify_exp03_pins`: **12/12 match**, reviewed commit `62c9107b4150e44c4ac410ff4cab359c1e71cc10`.\n- Copied all 12 pinned files into scratch, verified them, then altered copied `tools/per_sample_metrics.py`: refusal correctly names the altered file.\n- Normal array corruption and `complete=false`: refused.\n- Canonical noncontiguous subset coverage: passes existing comparator test.\n- Historical missing/duplicate indices, reordered query strings, and manifest mismatch: refused.\n- One nonzero-angle NaN: **nonreplication (validity mismatch)**, exactly one mismatch, surviving numerical differences zero.\n- Identical protocol with different execution IDs: summarizer refuses.\n- Same-device different batch size or tool implementation hash: summarizer refuses.\n- Valid fixture’s offline waveform/acoustic comparison: passes.\n\nEvidence: [adversarial_results.json](/home/yixunhu/codespace/xRIR_code_wt10/.review-round1/compare/adversarial_results.json), [reproduction script](/home/yixunhu/codespace/xRIR_code_wt10/.review-round1/compare/adversarial_compare.py), [test log](/home/yixunhu/codespace/xRIR_code_wt10/.review-round1/compare/pytest_compare.log).\n\nScope clarification: the diff actually adds **seven** files, including `tests/exp10_fixture.py`; the MAIN round prompt explicitly permits small test fixtures, so this is a discrepancy in the six-file claim, rather than an unauthorized implementation addition.\n\nComparator verdict: **changes required; not approved** until findings 1–3 are fixed.\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"\n[56] tool exec call: text(await tools.write_stdin({session_id:7098,chars:\"\",yield_time_ms:1000,max_output_tokens:2000}));\ntext(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"tail -10 .review-round1/main/smoke.log; ls .review-round1/main/smoke; git status --short; cat .review-round1/bootstrap/a3_results.json\",\"max_output_tokens\":2200}));\n\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"\n[57] tool exec result: Script completed\nWall time 0.1 seconds\nOutput:\n\n{\"chunk_id\":\"cb1b80\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000001406,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":0,\"output\":\"\"}\n{\"chunk_id\":\"8591b9\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.00000782,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":994,\"output\":\"  warnings.warn(\\n/home/yixunhu/miniconda3/envs/xRIR/lib/python3.8/site-packages/torchvision/models/_utils.py:223: UserWarning: Arguments other than a weight enum or `None` for 'weights' are deprecated since 0.13 and may be removed in the future. The current behavior is equivalent to passing `weights=None`.\\n  warnings.warn(msg)\\n[16/16] 0.21 samples/s, eta 0.0 min\\n/home/yixunhu/miniconda3/envs/xRIR/lib/python3.8/site-packages/torch/functional.py:504: UserWarning: torch.meshgrid: in an upcoming release, it will be required to pass the indexing argument. (Triggered internally at ../aten/src/ATen/native/TensorShape.cpp:3483.)\\n  return _VF.meshgrid(tensors, **kwargs)  # type: ignore[attr-defined]\\ndone: 16 queries x 5 angles in 1.30 min (.review-round1/main/smoke)\\n/home/yixunhu/miniconda3/envs/xRIR/lib/python3.8/site-packages/torch/functional.py:641: UserWarning: stft with return_complex=False is deprecated. In a future pytorch release, stft will return complex tensors for all inputs, and return_complex=False will raise an error.\\nNote: you can still call torch.view_as_real on the complex output to recover the old return format. (Triggered internally at ../aten/src/ATen/native/SpectralOps.cpp:862.)\\n  return _VF.stft(input, n_fft, hop_length, win_length, window,  # type: ignore[attr-defined]\\nmeta.json\\nmetrics.json\\nper_sample.json\\nwav_k0.npy\\nwav_k128.npy\\nwav_k256.npy\\nwav_k384.npy\\nwav_k64.npy\\n?? .review-round1/\\n?? checkpoints\\n{\\n  \\\"seed0\\\": {\\n    \\\"n\\\": 32,\\n    \\\"unit\\\": null,\\n    \\\"mean_0\\\": 0.47235617590541124,\\n    \\\"mean_alpha\\\": 0.19764207783533316,\\n    \\\"mean_gap\\\": 1.0,\\n    \\\"exclusions\\\": {\\n      \\\"invalid_at_0\\\": 0,\\n      \\\"invalid_at_alpha\\\": 0,\\n      \\\"gap_invalid\\\"<truncated omitted_approx_tokens=\"138\" />son\\\": null\\n    },\\n    \\\"contributions\\\": {\\n      \\\"fraction_worse\\\": 0.34375,\\n      \\\"mean_positive_part\\\": 0.19764207783533314,\\n      \\\"mean_negative_part\\\": -0.4723561759054113\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"seed1\\\": {\\n    \\\"n\\\": 32,\\n    \\\"unit\\\": null,\\n    \\\"mean_0\\\": 0.47235617590541124,\\n    \\\"mean_alpha\\\": 0.19764207783533316,\\n    \\\"mean_gap\\\": 1.0,\\n    \\\"exclusions\\\": {\\n      \\\"invalid_at_0\\\": 0,\\n      \\\"invalid_at_alpha\\\": 0,\\n      \\\"gap_invalid\\\": 0,\\n      \\\"n_total\\\": 32,\\n      \\\"n_mask\\\": 32,\\n      \\\"excluded_total\\\": 0\\n    },\\n    \\\"unit_of_resampling\\\": \\\"query\\\",\\n    \\\"n_clusters\\\": null,\\n    \\\"gap\\\": {\\n      \\\"point\\\": 1.0,\\n      \\\"lo\\\": 1.0,\\n      \\\"hi\\\": 1.0\\n    },\\n    \\\"delta\\\": {\\n      \\\"point\\\": -0.274714098070078,\\n      \\\"lo\\\": -0.5601881589294494,\\n      \\\"hi\\\": 0.00021676560180172887\\n    },\\n    \\\"ratio\\\": {\\n      \\\"point\\\": -3.6401480922355343,\\n      \\\"lo\\\": null,\\n      \\\"hi\\\": null,\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"denominator uncertain\\\",\\n      \\\"zero_draw_fraction\\\": 0.0,\\n      \\\"reason\\\": \\\"the delta interval contains 0\\\"\\n    },\\n    \\\"contributions\\\": {\\n      \\\"fraction_worse\\\": 0.34375,\\n      \\\"mean_positive_part\\\": 0.19764207783533314,\\n      \\\"mean_negative_part\\\": -0.4723561759054113\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"convergence\\\": {\\n    \\\"delta\\\": {\\n      \\\"converged\\\": true,\\n      \\\"max_relative_movement\\\": 0.0210210381645469,\\n      \\\"zero_width\\\": false\\n    },\\n    \\\"gap\\\": {\\n      \\\"converged\\\": true,\\n      \\\"max_relative_movement\\\": null,\\n      \\\"zero_width\\\": true\\n    },\\n    \\\"ratio\\\": {\\n      \\\"converged\\\": \\\"not applicable\\\",\\n      \\\"max_relative_movement\\\": null,\\n      \\\"zero_width\\\": null\\n    },\\n    \\\"status_agrees\\\": false,\\n    \\\"converged\\\": true\\n  },\\n  \\\"headline\\\": {\\n    \\\"reportable\\\": false,\\n    \\\"point\\\": -3.6401480922355343,\\n    \\\"lower_bound\\\": -22.255005263640076,\\n    \\\"upper_bound\\\": -1.3177198241576975,\\n    \\\"reason\\\": \\\"predictions shift while net error improves\\\"\\n  }\\n}\"}\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"\n[58] assistant: Agent message from /root/outputs_review:\nMessage Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/outputs_review\nPayload:\n1. **Should-fix — controls can pass with missing or invalid evidence.** `tools/exp10_summarize.py:497–506,520`: the table checks only controls present in JSON; `np.nanmax` discards invalid per-query waveform/logspec differences. A fresh fixture with one null waveform and logspec difference returns `ok=True`. Removing declared `ctrl_full_turn` also returns `ok=True`. Minimal fix: validate the requested control set, required metrics, lengths, and finiteness before applying tolerances. Reproduced in `.review-round1/outputs/audit_controls.log`.\n\n2. **Should-fix — required interpretation labels are absent.** `tools/exp10_summarize.py:335–337,532,799–862`: T60 is plotted as `%` and ratios are reported without explaining that Δ uses GT-normalised percentage points while G uses baseline-prediction T60. Neither Markdown nor figures identify waveform/acoustic changes as model-plus-Griffin-Lim sensitivity or state that GL can amplify magnitude changes. Minimal fix: add explicit T60 denominator labels and the pipeline qualification to generated artifacts. The absolute-seconds T60 pair is also omitted from summaries; bootstrap reviewer covers this omission.\n\n3. **Should-fix — figures impute missing estimates as zero.** `tools/exp10_summarize.py:696–704`: `value or 0.0` converts `None` estimates and interval endpoints into zero-height bars. Reproduced with an empty EDT comparison cell: JSON/CSV remain null, but the figure draws both zero-valued bars and reports only `n = 0-24`, concealing which angle has no data. Minimal fix: omit unavailable bars/intervals, label that angle unavailable with its actual n, and preserve measured zeros separately.\n\n4. **Should-fix — Markdown drops required results already available in JSON.** `tools/exp10_summarize.py:816–817,856–862`: Metric 2 iterates only acoustic triples, omitting `log_mse` and `loss`; the room table omits room ratio estimates/intervals and convergence. Minimal fix: include accuracy-only metrics and render the stored room ratio/convergence fields.\n\n5. **Nit — malformed Markdown controls table and ineffective output assertion.** `tools/exp10_summarize.py:865–867` embeds unescaped `|dwave|`, `|dlogspec|`, and `|dacoustic|`, producing fourteen header cells versus eight separator/data cells. Escape the pipes or use Δ labels. `tests/test_exp10_summarize.py:528` ends with `or True`, making its output-content assertion unconditional; remove that bypass.\n\n**Verified**\n\n- Executed Python 3.8, CPU-only synthetic five-angle run fixtures and generated strict JSON, Markdown, CSV, individual PNG/PDF, and combined figures under `.review-round1/outputs/`.\n- Compared **all fields of all 16 plotted CSV rows** against values derived from the persisted canonical JSON: exact equality.\n- Inspected rendered figure: signed negative EDT bars, four panels including GL-free spectral shift, correct EDT seconds→milliseconds conversion, and exact “context only” historical-band label.\n- Changing `per_sample.json` after building a summary caused `write_outputs` to refuse publication.\n- Reproduced null→zero rendering and the two false-positive control checks.\n- Confirmed broader-population G omission: shared mask had n=23, G≈0.0016799763; all finite gaps had n=24, G≈4.168276644, with no standalone result. Parent/bootstrap reviewer already informed.\n- Artifacts: `.review-round1/outputs/audit_outputs.py`, `audit_outputs.log`, `audit_controls.py`, `audit_controls.log`, and `generated/`.\n\nThe known missing cylindrical band remains to be supplied in the planned fix round. Other declared figure deviations do not introduce a separate correctness concern.\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"\n[59] assistant: Agent message from /root/bootstrap_review:\nMessage Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/bootstrap_review\nPayload:\n1. **Should-fix — A3 status disagreement can produce an unwarranted improvement headline.** `tools/exp10_summarize.py:317–329` returns status-specific wording before checking convergence/status agreement. A reproducible 32-query, 10,000-resample fixture produces seed-0 Δ CI `[-0.5486593, -0.000216766]` and seed-1 CI `[-0.5601882, +0.000216766]`. Bounds converge, but statuses disagree; the headline still says “predictions shift while net error improves.” A3 requires “unresolved Monte Carlo uncertainty.” **Minimal fix:** check convergence and status agreement before substantive status wording. Reproduction: [.review-round1/bootstrap/review_a3.py](/home/yixunhu/codespace/xRIR_code_wt10/.review-round1/bootstrap/review_a3.py).\n\n2. **Should-fix — Canonical summary omits the separately labelled standalone G population.** `tools/exp10_summarize.py:439–456` computes acoustic G only on the shared comparison mask. With errors invalid for one query and finite gaps `[100,1,2,3]`, it reports paired `n=3, G=2` but omits standalone gap-finite `n=4, G=26.5`. Pilot `metrics.json` retains broader means, but the canonical summary/Markdown lacks the separately labelled readout required by §4. **Minimal fix:** add an explicitly labelled gap-finite G cell with its population, intervals, and convergence, preserving the paired-mask Δ/G/R cells.\n\n3. **Nit — A3 observed-zero reason depends incorrectly on bootstrap status.** `tools/exp10_summarize.py:247–254` attaches “observed delta = 0” only when status is `undefined`. A continuous 16-query fixture has observed Δ exactly zero and no exact-zero bootstrap draws; the null point ratio instead receives only “the delta interval contains 0.” **Minimal fix:** record the observed-zero point-estimate reason independently of denominator status.\n\nThe missing absolute-seconds T60 summary and T60/pipeline qualifications were independently corroborated; the output reviewer covers them. The comparator reviewer covers acceptance of mismatched `per_sample_sha256`.\n\n**Verified**\n\nExecuted Python 3.8.20 CPU-only adversarial scripts with `CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=\"\"`, writing exclusively under `.review-round1/bootstrap/`.\n\n- Independent 10,000-draw query oracle exactly matched Δ*, G*, R* using a shared mask and shared indices.\n- Independent expanded-query room oracle exactly matched unequal-size rooms and repeated-room multiplicities.\n- All-zero Δ, a single exact-zero draw, undefined precedence, null point ratio, identical zero-width convergence, and changed zero-width failure passed.\n- Duplicate protocol executions, same-device batch mismatch, and implementation-hash mismatch were refused.\n- Both findings above were actively reproduced.\n\nEvidence: [results.json](/home/yixunhu/codespace/xRIR_code_wt10/.review-round1/bootstrap/results.json), [a3_results.json](/home/yixunhu/codespace/xRIR_code_wt10/.review-round1/bootstrap/a3_results.json).\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"\n[60] tool exec call: text(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"env CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 PYTHONPATH=\\\"$PWD\\\" XRIR_DATA_PATH=/home/yixunhu/data_cache/AcousticRooms TMPDIR=\\\"$PWD/.review-round1/main/tmp\\\" MPLCONFIGDIR=\\\"$PWD/.review-round1/main/mpl\\\" XDG_CACHE_HOME=\\\"$PWD/.review-round1/main/cache\\\" /home/yixunhu/miniconda3/envs/xRIR/bin/python - <<'PY' > .review-round1/main/smoke-audit.log 2>&1\\nimport os,json,numpy as np,torch\\nfrom tools import exp10_compare as c, exp10_summarize as s\\nfrom tools.exp10_yaw_pilot import file_sha256,METRIC1_NAMES\\nroot='.review-round1/main'\\nrun=root+'/smoke'\\ntorch.set_num_threads(16)\\nm,p=c.load_run(run)\\nstrict=lambda path:json.load(open(path),parse_constant=lambda x:(_ for _ in ()).throw(ValueError(x)))\\nfor name in ('per_sample','metrics','meta'): strict(run+'/'+name+'.json')\\nassert m['complete'] is True and len(p['query'])==16 and p['index']==list(range(16))\\nassert m['per_sample_sha256']==file_sha256(run+'/per_sample.json')\\nassert m['metrics_sha256']==file_sha256(run+'/metrics.json')\\nfor name in METRIC1_NAMES:\\n    assert p['angles']['0'][name]==[0.0]*16,(name,p['angles']['0'][name])\\nfor name,entry in m['arrays'].items():\\n    w=np.load(run+'/'+name)\\n    assert w.shape==(16,9600) and w.dtype==np.float32\\n    assert np.all(w[:,9579:]==0)\\n    assert entry['sha256']==file_sha256(run+'/'+name)\\nfor k,cell in p['angles'].items():\\n    for measure in ('edt','c50','t60'):\\n        raw_p=np.asarray(cell[measure+'_pred'],dtype=float)\\n        raw_0=np.asarray(p['angles']['0'][measure+'_pred'],dtype=float)\\n        raw_g=np.asarray(p['gt'][measure+'_gt'],dtype=float)\\n        for ref,key in ((raw_g,measure+'_err'),(raw_0,measure+'_gap')):\\n            expected=np.abs(raw_p-ref)\\n     