ustic** halves of Metric 1, recomputed\\n     8\\t  from the stored ``wav_k<k>.npy`` arrays, must equal what the run recorded online (the\\n     9\\t  spectral halves are computed from the model's direct output and are not recoverable\\n    10\\t  from a finite-iteration Griffin-Lim waveform, so they are excluded by contract);\\n    11\\t* :func:`parity_exp03` -- the run's rows, aligned to exp_03's historical per-sample file\\n    12\\t  by canonical index, with the per-sample and paired differences that the plan's parity\\n    13\\t  criteria are read off (this module reports them; it does not decide a launch).\\n    14\\t\\n    15\\t    python tools/exp10_compare.py check-online <run-dir>\\n    16\\t    python tools/exp10_compare.py parity-exp03 <run-dir> <exp03-per-sample.json>\\n    17\\t    python tools/exp10_compare.py verify-pins [binding-report.json]\\n    18\\t\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    19\\tfrom __future__ import annotations\\n    20\\t\\n    21\\timport argparse\\n    22\\timport json\\n    23\\timport os\\n    24\\t\\n    25\\timport numpy as np\\n    26\\t\\n    27\\tfrom eval_unseen import Evaluator\\n    28\\tfrom tools.exp10_yaw_pilot import (\\n    29\\t    acoustic_gap,\\n    30\\t    file_sha256,\\n    31\\t    query_list_sha256,\\n    32\\t    waveform_gap,\\n    33\\t)\\n    34\\t\\n    35\\tREPO_ROOT = os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)))\\n    36\\tDEFAULT_BINDING_REPORT = os.path.join(REPO_ROOT, \\\"ckpt\\\", \\\"yaw_rotation\\\",\\n    37\\t   <truncated omitted_approx_tokens=\"7505\" />duled from the probe forecast |\\n\\n## 12. Round-3 amendments (binding; APPROVE WITH CHANGES)\\n\\n- **A1 — validity masks in the parity rule (§7).** An arm/angle/metric cell is an exp_03 replication only if the per-query validity masks of the new run and of exp_03 are **identical** on the compared population (probe rows, then the full split) and criteria (a)–(c) pass on the common-finite rows; any mask mismatch labels the cell \\\"nonreplication (validity mismatch)\\\" and is listed in the results. The historical Δ comparison population is the common-finite rows of that identical mask. Test: a fixture with one nonzero-angle NaN whose numerical differences would otherwise pass must be flagged.\\n- **A2 — execution identity (§5).** Two identifiers in meta and inside `per_sample.json`: `protocol_id` = sha256 over the complete protocol (checkpoint sha256, manifest hash, gl_seed, K, device, cudnn/TF32 flags, batch size and canonical padding, torch/numpy versions, sha256 of `tools/exp10_yaw_pilot.py`) and `execution_id` = a uuid4 + start timestamp minted once per `run`. Δ, G and R are computed from **one** `per_sample.json` whose `execution_id` matches its `meta.json` and whose bound waveform arrays' sha256s match. The summariser refuses (test 16) two executions with identical configuration, and same-device runs whose batch or implementation settings differ.\\n- **A3 — ratio point estimate and convergence (§1, §4).** If the observed Δ is exactly 0, the point ratio is null with reason \\\"observed Δ = 0\\\" (before any division); a headline multiple requires bound convergence **and** identical denominator status under seeds 0 and 1, otherwise the cell reports \\\"unresolved Monte Carlo uncertainty\\\". Fixtures for both.\\n- **A4 — `log_mse` contract (§4).** `log_mse` is exp_03's per-query mean over [F, T] of `(out − log(tgt_spec + 1e-8))²` (`eval_yaw_rotation.spectral_metrics`, not `per_sample_losses`, which returns loss / stft / decay only).\\n\"}\n\n[12] tool exec call: text(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"sed -n '1,90p' /home/yixunhu/codespace/xRIR_code/worklog/experiment_SOP.md; sed -n '37,60p' /home/yixunhu/codespace/xRIR_code/worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_10_yaw_pilot_claude/plan_yaw_pilot.md; nl -ba tests/test_exp10_summarize.py | sed -n '1,230p'; cat tests/exp10_fixture.py\",\"max_output_tokens\":17500}));\n\n\n[13] tool exec result: Script completed\nWall time 0.1 seconds\nOutput:\n\nWarning: truncated output (original token count: 12485)\nTotal output lines: 1\n\n{\"chunk_id\":\"023510\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000008554,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":12039,\"output\":\"# Experiment SOP (portable)\\n\\nA generalizable standard operating procedure for AI-assisted research experiments. Drop this file into any project and reference it from that project's `CLAUDE.md` (e.g. \\\"Follow `worklog/experiment_SOP.md` for all experiment work\\\"). Written for Claude Code, but the roles are model-agnostic.\\n\\n## Roles (three-model separation of duties)\\n\\n| Role | Who | Duty |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| **Planner / Analyst** | The main-session model (strongest reasoning tier; currently Claude Fable 5.1) | Writes plans, judges reliability, writes analyses. Does NOT write implementation code directly. |\\n| **Coder** | The strongest coding model at its highest reasoning setting — **currently Claude Opus 5 at max effort, a separate subagent launched from the main session (Agent tool, model `opus`) working in a dedicated git worktree (per Yixun 2026-09-15; 2026-09-12 → 2026-09-15 it was OpenAI Codex `gpt-6-astra` at Ultra via `codex exec`; before that a Claude Opus 4.8 max-effort subagent)** | Implements exactly what the approved plan specifies. |\\n| **Reviewer** | **The opposite model family from the Coder** (mandatory cross-model review; see reciprocity note below). | Reviews all newly written code; review is saved, not just read. If the reviewer is unavailable, say so — never silently substitute. |\\n\\n> **Reviewer reciprocity — no model reviews its own code.** The Reviewer is always the opposite model family from the **Coder**. With the current roles (Planner Claude Fable 5.1, Coder Claude Opus 5; per Yixun 2026-09-15), the code Reviewer is **OpenAI Codex `gpt-6-astra` at Ultra** (`codex exec -s read-only` in the worktree; its final message is saved as the review file with the identity header). When the<truncated omitted_approx_tokens=\"9039\" />l index to list twice