ut lines: 4\n\n{\"i\":0,\"status\":\"fulfilled\",\"value\":{\"chunk_id\":\"46d208\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000002398,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":6453,\"output\":\"# Plan — exp_10 `yaw_pilot` (xRIR analogue of FLAC exp_02 `yaw_noninvariance`)\\n\\n**Planner:** Claude Fable 5.1 (session xrir-code-25). **Coder:** Claude Opus 5 (Agent, worktree `xRIR_code_wt10`, branch `exp10-yaw-pilot`). **Reviewer:** OpenAI Codex `gpt-6-astra` at **ultra** (SOP setting; round 1 ran at xhigh, see §10). **Date:** 2026-09-26. **Status:** **v3.1 — APPROVED WITH CHANGES** by the round-3 review at ultra (`yaw_pilot_codex_plan_review_round3.md`; its 3 should-fixes + 1 nit are the binding amendments A1–A4 of §12). v3 was the round-2 revision at ultra (`yaw_pilot_codex_plan_review_round2.md`, REQUEST CHANGES, 1 blocker + 5 should-fixes + 2 nits; §11 maps them); v2 was the round-1 revision (`yaw_pilot_codex_plan_review.md`; §10). v1 kept as `plan_yaw_pilot_v1_superseded.md`.\\n\\n## 1. Question and stance\\n\\n**Question (Yixun, 2026-09-26).** Mimicking FLAC's exp_02 pilot: when the *conditioning* of the released xRIR checkpoint is yaw-rotated on the AcousticRooms unseen split, how much does the **prediction itself move** (Metric 1, P_α vs P_0, no GT) compared with how much **accuracy vs GT changes** (Metric 2)? FLAC's finding: \\\"predictions move ~5× more than net accuracy loses\\\".\\n\\n**Stance.** A **descriptive pilot**, like FLAC's: paired means with query-level bootstrap intervals; no confirmatory hypotheses (exp_03 already ran the Bonferroni-adjusted H1/H2 tests on Metric 2 for K = 8). Pre-registered readouts, per arm, angle and metric:\\n\\n- **R1** signed accuracy change Δ(α) = mean(e_α − e_0) vs GT, and prediction shift G(α) = mean(g_α), each with a 95 % paired query-level percentile bootstrap interval, on the **shared comparison mask** of §4; paired-va<truncated omitted_approx_tokens=\"9039\" /> Live exp_03 pins matched **12/12**; copied-source tampering was refused.\\n- **Reports:** generated JSON/Markdown/CSV/PNG/PDF; all fields of 16 independently audited plotted CSV rows matched canonical JSON. Verified cylindrical SDs against the canonical five-seed record.\\n- **CPU smoke:** batch 0, 16 queries, five angles, three fresh controls; `check-online`, `parity-exp03`, and the default 10,000-draw summariser completed. All stored waveforms and numerical per-sample results exactly matched the prior isolated round-1 smoke.\\n\\n| Smoke check | Observed |\\n|---|---:|\\n| k=0 gaps; control deviations; offline gap differences | Exactly 0 |\\n| Exp_03 EDT/T60 maximum differences | 0 |\\n| Exp_03 C50 maximum difference | `4.6491623e-5 dB` |\\n| Exp_03 logspec maximum difference | `6.2820358e-6` |\\n| Validity mismatches | 0 |\\n| Required comparisons missing | `[]` |\\n| CPU batch-16 forward | **5.979 s** |\\n| Inversion per query/angle | **45.0 ms** |\\n\\nThe declared methodological/testing deviations are sound. The original stochastic A3 reproduction also passes, supporting the deterministic regression fixture.\\n\\nThe disposable clone’s **`--no-ff --no-commit` merge onto main `9c7dd1c`**, a descendant of `e755792`, completed without conflicts and added exactly the seven permitted files. The clone was deleted.\\n\\nEvidence is retained under [.review-round2/](/home/yixunhu/codespace/xRIR_code_wt10/.review-round2), including the [smoke audit](/home/yixunhu/codespace/xRIR_code_wt10/.review-round2/main/smoke-audit.log), [adversarial results](/home/yixunhu/codespace/xRIR_code_wt10/.review-round2/compare/adversarial_results.json), and [merge rehearsal](/home/yixunhu/codespace/xRIR_code_wt10/.review-round2/main/merge.log). Tracked files and checkpoints remained untouched; no GPU was used.\\n\\n**Exact blocking list: remaining finding 1 above—round-1 finding 6’s overlapping figure qualification. Findings 2–3 are nonblocking nits. Not approved for merge.**\\n\"}}\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"\n[11] assistant: The prior review left one merge-blocking issue—the overlapping footer—and two nonblocking figure nits. I’m checking those directly. A parallel audit is running the suites and merge rehearsal; I’ll compare round-2 and round-3 non-figure outputs at the same bootstrap count.\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"\n[12] tool spawn_agent call: {\"task_name\":\"data_artists\",\"message\":\"gAAAAABquF9urFoWaLWRfC2DOzpACCItgykOWVSMXLlWIl4hBnJfdmE97FHgn24p6Uhn9aLDYpucOtzY3EIBokNbY4C910cWsRieM16MtSgHKFGrbAp0T2xu4AEojRIzivmBnhTjzxohKDzRx5N9R-_MtpnAz2GLwo416CcfVzvQTqZe3bDPB47UkHrOoraJbCUodH0g6U0Yg9An9QjsEKXqLYWEq5UKm42QoIHUGTbxbhXC82ArYiYDJxw9iEDUWt4cfJwnzrE2G_KpXRdfcYssUEIjJiH-IgYzGbYkOaF6AML5YsKvGyT9G7lkQ91kNyqfcrSMpyY1YpX9Fpgc-8qmULQJv-UtAm47h9C1aenmw0Ed633KNM97cR6pxmeSX2V-FRnJC_cCbb1fmUtGzsLvuDBruzQEqjA768soc2BxkTWJRzhmiPdzH5OOrWa6jgj-7ss_a42phd_IF3TXzr3gIrRc7NjcAoFHUvoirdC2T-TdPBEIJkbOI_qCQ9C4kO68whBSHSqDD9mOLCrZ08RY4FmC6N4iwGB4HRv_2sE5eChPhCZXuCadQ_XBOJ5Bdlza9mw1k7YEeBmZ20Ubz9m35PUmnB04wkuMb6rwYkC3Ey98cwS4_0xjU1xD5acQHoxMSYE8qDrBjSY-adb0fNB-UN62O3dybIZ1lGA8Dehamje35iauV21NZI6IsKztRL-N20kensem3tDFVlt4IPH3u4-Chc1aBmU0bvV2Xkno4LdSFKW9Sh_vX5tVJmS2ZYeMHeHsSWO-PS_Em--btpEy18YiFgTi34v3iPnS8o6EfMEljFVhcQbKuxFxcPN5RgA3t5RFZUiTH9SKL3Cea0mdas39IhsJ4I3mej5OluuCnDSdKcFKnQqFAzkRebfDISHa8XUNq-CmF89H1YXXXJaqXgt0MCjpsPzakxm_awxxOIeMxP5ZHx-ArDJyj77zxjafs5aFzSAE4_2Lv_zqST-_RwavNC_U-U9GcCi0wtfGehskBEJdaM92Mbeg5OooZVERkjGKP8FyObFGua7sjeI390yHR27h2U4-k-4TRLQKhpEC-wUZknYn1-WPB5vjooSXBrIYHky1foBS780joF1-oPLYg1EJmkVE-O7wjNVh6kirG8vRASV7DwAoyexjGu4MDeWHSBrXizOncvPN3zGKhiLWXpOc5lExgMpot7Z6sNiu88cIax1SbDPBfCf94uJbQuFYubAgTEqs-dbQ8VQNs8a6wDfdt8QZqX0J7ysHetp7Cjhi_vYe2HgNLgv1sG-nc3cBxC2l5RgjjMd2KCGUW0RHk33QSC_rVutGYlLnE6inCTsQ9HBz0ELXxtburjoKEJVXFjYD3jq1nTsmIP6e7pyfzW20zfU8IfC9B3aCAGTnUa-xlto=\"}\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"\n[13] tool spawn_agent result: {\"task_name\":\"/root/data_artists\"}\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"\n[14] tool exec call: const r = await Promise.allSettled([\ntools.exec_command({cmd:\"git diff ea24dd1..